From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:04:10 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 46/63] Meridian: shortcuts and menu commands work again; no
 rubber band; greeting font
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Meridian's commands (39700-39725) have no ActionItem, and with
  UseActionsForBrowserCommands (on by default in M158) the command updater
  treated them as unsupported and disabled: every Meridian menu item and
  shortcut was dead (⌘⌥←/→, ⌃1-9, ⌘S, ⌘D…), and ⌘1-9 / ⌃Tab ran the raw tab
  strip's actions instead of the sidebar's order. They are now enabled in
  normal windows and handed to the sidebar before the updater.
- Space switching is reserved, like ⌘T: a page can't keep ⌘⌥←/→ or ⌃1-9.
- The browser frame page no longer rubber-bands on a swipe.
- Non-Latin greetings in the welcome tour use a system face (the script
  faces have no Cyrillic).
- Tests: TestKeyPress (--meridian-test-keys, temp profile only) sends a real
  NSEvent through AppKit, so shortcuts are tested end to end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
